# Veyra Prime — see docs/PLATFORM_STANDARD.md §3.2
#
# Size budget, measured 2026-07-29 (git-lfs is NOT installed on this machine):
#   src + content + docs + scripts + server + worker + migrations   ≈   3 MB  → plain git
#   public/models 104M · audio 147M · textures 123M · site 26M      ≈ 400 MB → Drive-only, symlinked
#   masters/                                                        ≈ 266 MB → Drive-only, symlinked
#   assets/ (raw generator output)                                  ≈ 2.2 GB → Drive-only, symlinked
#   dist/, node_modules/                                            ≈ 579 MB → never
#
# Binary asset trees stay on the Drive (synced, backed up, offline-pinned) and are
# symlinked into the build tree by ops/scripts/bootstrap.sh. That keeps git fast for
# the code — which is what version control is actually needed for here: the sweeping
# multi-file refactors in docs/CONVERGENCE_PLAN.md §1.2.
#
# If a second contributor joins, install git-lfs and move public/ into it. Until then
# a 3 MB repo that clones instantly beats a 3.4 GB one nobody wants to branch.

# ── build output and dependencies ─────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
dist-release/
.vite/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ── local service state ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.wrangler/
.dev.vars

# ── secrets ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# .env.production is tracked BY EXCEPTION: it holds only the two public VITE_ service
# URLs (verified 2026-07-29) and a fresh clone cannot build a correct production
# bundle without it. CI gate 6 greps every build artefact for secrets, and any secret
# added to this file would be caught there. Do not put a key in it.
!.env.production

# ── binary asset trees: Drive-only, symlinked in by bootstrap.sh ──────────────
# Generator masters and shipped binaries. They live in $MW_ROOT (synced +
# offline-pinned) and are the provenance record for every shipped asset.
assets/
masters/
assets-source/tripo-raw/
assets-source/dcc/
assets-source/audio-master/

# public/ is PARTIALLY tracked: the big binary subdirs are ignored, but the small
# load-bearing files are NOT. public/.assetsignore in particular is what keeps the
# Cloudflare Worker under its 25 MiB/file limit — losing it breaks deploys.
public/models/
public/audio/
public/textures/
public/site/
# (public/fonts/ is 188K and stays tracked; public/.assetsignore stays tracked)

# ── capture and scratch ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.site-shots/
*.trace
playwright-report/
test-results/

# ── macOS / Drive litter (11 .DS_Store present as of 2026-07-29) ──────────────
.DS_Store
Icon?
~$*
*.tmp
*.swp

# ── Drive conflict duplicates — these must NEVER be committed ─────────────────
# Drive resolves a two-machine conflict by writing "file (1).ts". A duplicated .ts
# that still compiles is a silent bug factory. CI also fails the build on these.
*\ \(?\).*
